--==================================================================
--  Feed A Mosquito  |  Matcha LuaVM menu tab (UI.AddTab)
--
--  v8.7  -  EGG RARITY AND VALUE, READ CORRECTLY
--
--  TWO WRONG ASSUMPTIONS FROM v8.6, NOW FIXED
--    1. There is no Coin field in MosquitoConfig. It does not exist.
--       The real fields are Id, Name, Rarity, Icon, Prefab, EggIcon,
--       EggBaseScale, MinScale, MaxScale, MinIncome, MaxIncome,
--       Damage, MaxBlood, Price, HatchTime.
--    2. The area is NOT the egg's rarity. Probed live: an
--       IceMosquitoEgg sat inside UncommonArea while its own billboard
--       displayed "Rare". Rarity comes from the egg itself.
--
--  WHERE THE TWO VALUES NOW COME FROM
--    RARITY  - every egg model has a BillboardGui named EggGui
--              containing a TextLabel named "Rarity". That label is
--              what the game shows you in world, so it is read
--              directly (e.g. "Uncommon", "Rare", "Epic"). If a
--              label is missing, the area name is used as a fallback.
--    VALUE   - MosquitoConfig's Price field, keyed by the mosquito id.
--              The egg model name minus its "Egg" suffix is that id:
--                  BlueMosquitoEgg  ->  BlueMosquito  ->  Price 200
--                  FireMosquitoEgg  ->  FireMosquito  ->  Price 30000
--              Prices decompiled from the config: Common 100,
--              Uncommon 200, Rare 2000, Epic 30000, Legendary 300000.
--              These are the game's own numbers, not estimates.
--
--  PANEL LAYOUT (unchanged from v8.5)
--      left  PANEL_X = 300   boss name, HP bar, hp / max
--      right EGG_X  = 634    egg name, rarity + price
--    Both use the game's own 40,40,50 backdrop and bold text, colour
--    coded per rarity.
--
--  Drawing rules followed (Matcha has no GUI objects at all)
--    - fixed pools created once: 6 boss rows, 4 egg rows, 2 backdrops.
--      Nothing is created in the render loop.
--    - ONE RenderStepped connection total.
--    - boss scan cached 0.6 s, egg scan cached 1.0 s.
--    - every Drawing removed in stop().
--
--  Hit logic unchanged from v8.2, which works:
--    - AttackPart is the only thing written: shrink to 2 studs to end
--      every contact, grow back to map size to begin a new one, which
--      fires the tool's TouchTransmitter
--    - PlaySound("SwingSound") + Attack on the LIVE tool actor from
--      the tool's ActorId value
--    - no mouse input, no equip or unequip, nothing reparented
--    - bosses and eggs are read only
--
--  Auto Health / Auto Collect / Kill Farm are the three toggles.
--  Stop with _G.FeedAMosquito.stop().
--==================================================================
